# Reader-Writer Problem

## Use Case
### Concurrent Product Inventory Management

This project demonstrates the Reader-Writer synchronization problem
in a product inventory system where multiple users may access
inventory information concurrently.

## Concept

- Multiple readers can access shared data simultaneously.
- A writer requires exclusive access to modify the shared data.
- Read-write synchronization prevents inconsistent data access.

## Concepts Used

- Threads
- Reader-Writer Problem
- Read-Write Locks
- Mutual Exclusion
- Critical Section
- Process Synchronization
- Concurrent Access
